<interrogationes unitas="pictor_documentum">

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what is a pictor document, and where is the picture actually stored?
    <responsum symbolum="PictorDocumentum pictor_documentum_proiectio historia_actum" via="lib/pictor_documentum.worklog.md include/historia.h">The
      truth is the append-only log of acts in a volumen (strokes, layer
      changes, pasted images); the bitmap is a projection rebuilt from
      the nearest checkpoint plus the live acts after it. The log
      machinery (branches, checkpoints, cursor, undo, redo, verify) is
      historia; this library only knows how to paint an act into RGBA
      layers.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I open an existing drawing, or create one if it does not exist yet?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_aperire pictor_documentum_creare pictor_documenta_enumerare" via="lib/pictor_applicatio.c">Try
      pictor_documentum_aperire(piscina, intern, volumen, spatium)
      first; it reads the size from the plagula SPATIUM/documentum (or
      documentum for an empty spatium) and returns NIHIL if that is
      missing or gives a zero size. Only then call pictor_documentum_creare with a size
      and checkpoint interval (0 or less means LXIV): it does not check
      for an existing document and rewrites the manifest.
      pictor_documenta_enumerare lists every spatium in a
      volume.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I record a brush stroke so it is saved and can be undone?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_actum pictor_documentum_revocare pictor_documentum_reficere" via="lib/pictor_actiones.c">Pass
      the stroke as STML text to pictor_documentum_actum: an ictus
      element with instrumentum, color (palette index 0-15), magnitudo
      and optional color_secundus, exemplar, semen and stratum, holding
      punctum x y [t] children. It appends, paints and checkpoints when
      due, returning the seq (greater than 0) or 0 if refused.
      pictor_documentum_revocare and _reficere are undo and redo; a new
      act after an undo starts a branch, so nothing is ever
      truncated.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what tools can an ictus use, and how big is each one?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_disci_pixelum pictor_lineam_ambulare pictor_gutta">Absent
      or unknown instrumentum is the brush: a disc of diameter
      magnitudo at every point of the Bresenham line between points
      (sizes up to III are full squares). linea is the brush with two
      points. aspergillum sprays single pixels in a disc of radius
      PICTOR_ASPERGILLI_RADIUS x magnitudo, PICTOR_GUTTAE_PUNCTO x
      magnitudo per point plus more for dwell time, seeded by semen so
      replay is identical. spongia erases a PICTOR_SPONGIAE_LATUS x
      magnitudo square to transparent and ignores colour and
      pattern.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can a stroke that goes off the edge of the canvas wrap around or hang?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_actum pictor_lineam_ambulare" via="lib/pictor_documentum.worklog.md">No
      longer. Point coordinates are signed, and every segment is
      clipped to the canvas (Cohen-Sutherland in s64, widened by the
      stamp size) before it is walked, so a drag off the edge stops
      there. Before 2026-10-08 negative points were cast to the
      UNSIGNED i32 and a line ran to the opposite edge, or effectively
      forever.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I add, delete, reorder or hide layers?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_actum pictor_documentum_stratum pictor_documentum_numerus_stratorum PictorStratum">Append
      stratum acts with pictor_documentum_actum: actio novum id supra,
      deletum id, ordo ids (bottom first, must be a permutation of
      every layer), visibile id valor. Layers are named by id, not
      index; supra unknown or 0 puts the new layer on top. Invalid acts
      (duplicate id, deleting the last layer, more than
      PICTOR_STRATA_MAXIMA = XVI layers) are logged but change nothing.
      Read layers bottom first with pictor_documentum_stratum(doc,
      index).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why did my stroke get a sequence number but nothing appeared?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_actum PictorStratum">Acts
      are appended first and painted second, and painting ignores what
      it cannot apply: an ictus whose stratum id does not exist (absent
      means layer 1), a colour outside 0-15 (it means leave the pixel
      untouched), or an act whose root element is not ictus, stratum
      or imago. A stroke into a hidden layer IS painted but is not
      composited until the layer is shown. The seq only says the act
      was logged.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what does pictor_documentum_proiectio return, and does it blend layers?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_proiectio pictor_documentum_sigillum_compositi_hex">The
      COMPOSITE as an Imago that shares memory with doc->tabula, so it
      changes with the next act; copy it if you need a snapshot. It is
      the theme background colour, then each visible layer from the
      bottom, where any pixel with non-zero alpha replaces the one
      below: no alpha blending.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why are there two seals, and why can the composite seal change with the theme?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_sigillum_hex pictor_documentum_sigillum_compositi_hex pictor_documentum_verificare" via="lib/pictor_documentum.worklog.md">pictor_documentum_sigillum_hex
      hashes the document state (layer count, ids, visibility and every
      layer's pixels); pictor_documentum_verificare replays from nothing
      and compares it. pictor_documentum_sigillum_compositi_hex hashes
      the visible pixels, which include the background: that is
      thema_color(COLOR_BACKGROUND), not stored in the acts, so every
      drawing renders on today's theme background.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I paste an image into a drawing as a new layer?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_imaginem_aptare pictor_documentum_imaginem_inserere">pictor_imaginem_aptare
      fits the RGBA image inside the canvas keeping the aspect (small
      images are scaled UP), centres it, dithers it to the 16 Aquinas
      colours with Atkinson and marks alpha below CXXVIII as 0xFF
      (transparent). pictor_documentum_imaginem_inserere then stores
      the deflated indices as a volume massa and logs stratum novum plus
      imago as one conjoined group (one undo removes both), returning
      the new layer id (highest id + 1) or 0, which includes a full
      document of PICTOR_STRATA_MAXIMA layers. Only the first act's
      result is checked: if the imago act fails to append, the id is
      still returned. Replay never reruns the dithering. Caution (audit
      2026-10-18, unfixed): when that imago act fails, the log keeps an
      empty layer and a dangling coniunctio note, so the user's NEXT
      unrelated act is conjoined to the layer creation and one undo
      removes both.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how does a pending paste with an A/B choice work before it is committed?
    <responsum symbolum="pictor_documentum_glutinationem_parare pictor_documentum_glutinationem_confirmare pictor_documentum_glutinationem_abicere pictor_documentum_glutinationem_radere PictorGlutinatio">pictor_documentum_glutinationem_parare
      fits the image once and dithers it twice (A Atkinson, B
      dithering_exemplaria) into doc->glutinatio, OUTSIDE the log: no
      acts, no undo. A failed parare leaves any earlier pending paste
      alone. _radere paints a mask that shows the other mode;
      _confirmare(modus, supra) inserts the mixed result as a layer;
      _abicere drops it. Caution (audit 2026-10-18, unfixed): if the
      imago act inside the insert fails to append, _confirmare still
      gets a non-zero layer id, drops the pending paste and leaves an
      empty layer instead of the image.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
